    "text": "To determine the total amount of money Meghan had, we need to calculate the value of each type of bill separately and then sum these values.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the value of the $100 bills:\nMeghan has 2 $100 bills.\nThe value of the $100 bills is:\n\\[ 2 \\times 100 = 200 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nNext, let's calculate the value of the $50 bills:\nMeghan has 5 $50 bills.\nThe value of the $50 bills is:\n\\[ 5 \\times 50 = 250 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nThen, let's calculate the value of the $10 bills:\nMeghan has 10 $10 bills.\nThe value of the $10 bills is:\n\\[ 10 \\times 10 = 100 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nNow, we sum the values of all the bills to find the total amount of money Meghan had:\n\\[ 200 + 250 + 100 = 550 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nTherefore, the total amount of money Meghan had is \\(\\boxed{550}\\).",
